      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-curved-charge-action-variation",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Fixed-endpoint curved charge variation",
        "statement": "Let $(M,g,N)$ be a smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature $(-,+,+,+)$ ([[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]). Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the canonical tangent-bundle smooth structure, as required for the metric-selected Levi–Civita connection $\\nabla$ of [[thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative]]. Let $O\\subseteq M$ be open and let $A$ be a $C^2$ covector field on $O$; define the $C^1$ two-form $F=dA$ by $F_{ab}=\\partial_aA_b-\\partial_bA_a$ in each chart. Fix constants $c>0$, $m>0$ and $q\\in\\mathbb R$. Let $z:[a,b]\\to O$ be a $C^2$ future-directed timelike curve, where $a<b$ are proper-time values in seconds and $U=dz/d\\tau$ satisfies $g(U,U)=-c^2$. For every $C^2$ fixed-endpoint variation $z_\\epsilon$ through timelike curves in $O$, with variation field $J=\\partial_\\epsilon z_\\epsilon|_{\\epsilon=0}$ and $J(a)=J(b)=0$, define\n\n$$S[z_\\epsilon]=-mc\\int_a^b\\sqrt{-g(\\partial_\\tau z_\\epsilon,\\partial_\\tau z_\\epsilon)}\\,d\\tau+q\\int_a^b A(\\partial_\\tau z_\\epsilon)\\,d\\tau.$$\n\nThen the first variation is\n\n$$\\delta S=\\int_a^b\\left[-m\\,g(J,\\nabla_UU)+qF(J,U)\\right]d\\tau.$$\n\nConsequently, $z$ is stationary under all local chart-supported fixed-endpoint variations if and only if\n\n$$m(\\nabla_UU)_a=qF_{ab}U^b,$$\n\nequivalently $m\\nabla_UU=qF^\\sharp(U)$, where $F^\\sharp(v)$ is defined by $g(F^\\sharp(v),w)=F(w,v)$. The statement is local to a potential domain; no global potential is assumed.",
        "deps": [
          "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
          "thm-gr-compact-metric-and-timelike-curve-variation",
