      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-external-charge-local-ivp",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "External Lorentz ODE local well-posedness",
        "statement": "Let $(M,g,N)$ be a smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature $(-,+,+,+)$; assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for its canonical tangent-bundle smooth structure, so the metric-selected Levi–Civita connection $\\nabla$ exists by [[thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative]]. Let $O\\subseteq M$ be open and let $F$ be a $C^1$ alternating covariant two-tensor field on $O$ (a two-form); define $F^\\sharp$ by $g(F^\\sharp(v),w)=F(w,v)$. Fix $m,c>0$, $q\\in\\mathbb R$, an event $x_0\\in O$, and $U_0\\in T_{x_0}M$ with $g(U_0,U_0)=-c^2$ future directed. Then the initial-value problem\n\n$$\\dot x=U,\\qquad \\nabla_UU=(q/m)F^\\sharp(U),\\qquad (x(\\tau_0),U(\\tau_0))=(x_0,U_0)$$\n\nhas a unique local $C^2$ solution on an open proper-time interval containing $\\tau_0$. Any two solutions with these initial data agree on every connected part of their common domain containing $\\tau_0$. Along the solution, $g(U,U)=-c^2$ and $U$ remains future directed. The result is local; it asserts no completeness or global existence for arbitrary external fields.",
        "deps": [
          "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
          "thm-picard-lindelof-local-existence-and-uniqueness",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem",
          "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
