        "dependency_level": 3,
        "physical_scope": "An adopted classical polarization transport law for a charged massive test body in a prescribed external field, with Lorentz-force translation. The curved-spacetime form is an independent model extension; it is not inferred from the flat homogeneous-field BMT paper, from covariance alone or from experiments. No quantum-spin ontology or measured value of the gyromagnetic ratio is asserted."
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-external-charge-action-equivalence",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Stationary charged action and Lorentz force",
        "statement": "Assume the charged test-body quantities and local potential domain of [[def-rpm-charge-spin-model]], the flat-space sign convention of [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]], and the adopted fixed-endpoint action postulate [[post-rpm-external-charge-action]], and assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the canonical tangent-bundle smooth structure. For a finite $C^2$ future-timelike curve segment $z:[a,b]\\to O$ in that domain, where $a<b$ are proper-time endpoints, and the local $C^2$ fixed-endpoint variations of the postulate, choose the orientation-preserving parameter $\\lambda=\\tau$; the segment is stationary for the adopted action if and only if\n\n$$m\\nabla_UU=qF^\\sharp(U),\\qquad (\\nabla_UU)_a=\\frac qm F_{ab}U^b.$$\n\nThis is a model deduction: it establishes the equation equivalent to stationarity of the postulated functional, not the physical truth of the postulate.",
